      <p class="_abstract">Determine which identity providers are in your cluster. For more information about supported identity providers, see "Supported identity providers" in <em>Authentication and authorization</em>.</p>
      <p>After you know which providers are configured, you can inspect the <code>openshift-authentication</code> namespace to determine if there are potential issues.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check the events in the <code>openshift-authentication</code> namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get events -n openshift-authentication --sort-by='.metadata.creationTimestamp'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check the pods in the <code>openshift-authentication</code> namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get pod -n openshift-authentication "} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Optional: If you need more information, check the logs of one of the running pods by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc logs -n openshift-authentication <pod_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
